---
import AgencyLayout from '../layouts/AgencyLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<AgencyLayout title="Testing a Prototype Before Development — Expresiv" description="A studio note on choosing a task for a prototype, testing it with the people who will use it, and taking the findings into development.">
  <PageIntro section="Studio journal" href="/blog" lead="Testing a" accent="prototype." summary="Before you build a complete product, try one important task with the people who will use it."/>
  <article class="article-body wrap">
    <h2>Choose a task someone can finish</h2><p>For a customer portal, that might be finding an unpaid invoice and checking when it’s due. Include the screens and information needed to finish that job. Other features can wait.</p>
    <h2>Watch where the work slows down</h2><p>Give someone a realistic starting point and ask them to talk through what they would do. Watch what they look for, what they misread and where they leave the intended path. A hesitation can reveal as much as a failed task.</p>
    <h2>Take the findings into the build</h2><p>Revise the labels, order or interaction and try the same task again. Keep a short record of what changed so the developer understands the reasoning when implementing the flow.</p>
  </article>
</AgencyLayout>
